# Two Core Patterns of BitMask DP
        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      1 -> Dp over subSets :
        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
           
            // dp[mask] = best answer for this subset
        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        @Exaplaination using Question :->
        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        you have n people and n jobs.
        cost[i][j] = cost if person : does job j 
        Each person must be assigned exactly one job and each job can be used at most once. minimize total cost.
        
        constains : n <= 20

        we want to assign jobs to person : 0 --> n-1
        Total masks = 2^n

        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        @ step 1 :->
        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
           ---- Try to think what information do I need to make future decision
           
                ---Suppose we go person by person in order :-> 0 1 2 3 _ _ _ _ n-1
                ---At some point , we are at person i , and some jobs are already taken

          ----- We can  encoded "Which jobs are already taken" using a bitmask

                ---Mask -> if i-th bit is 1 , job i is already assigned  
                ---Number of assigned job = pop count of mask

          ----- if we assign jobs in order of persons ,than :->

                --- When mask has k bit set , that means we have already assignd jobs to the first k people
                --- So i = pop count of mask 

          ----- so we can define :->

                --- dp[mask] = minimum total cost to assign jobs to the first pop count of mask people, using exactly the jobs in mask.



         $Base Case :-> 
          -------------

              --- dp[0] = 0 (no person assigned , no jobs used , cost = 0)

          $Answer :->
          
              --- we want all n people assigned ,so all n jobs used : mask = (1 << n) - 1

              --- answer is dp[(1 << n)-1].

        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        @ step 2 :->      
        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

          ---- From current mask :
            
               Let i = pop count of mask -> next person to assign
               Try to assign some free jobs j (bit j = 0  in mask)

          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
          ---- Transition :->
          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

               for(int mask = 0 ; mask < (1 << n) ; mask++){
                 int i == pop count of mask

                 if(i >= n){
                    continue;
                 }

                 for(int j = 0 ; j < n ; j++){
                  if(!mask & (i << j)){
                    int newMask = mask | (1 << j){
                      dp[newMask] = Math.min(dp[newMask] , ,dp[mask]+ cost[i][j]);
                    }
                  }
                 }
               }     








