$$$$$$$$$ When to Use It (The Key Indicators)


Small Constraints: The number of items, nodes, or people (N) is small (e.g., N ≤ 20). 
Standard arrays or sets cannot store all subsets, but a single integer can.Subset/Combination 
Tracking: You need to track exactly which items have been "visited," "used," or "assigned" in a specific state.
Exponential Solution Required: The problem has overlapping 
subproblems and optimal substructure, but standard DP states don't provide enough history.